//! The `z-index` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the z-order
//! of a [positioned](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/position)
//! element and its descendants or flex and grid items. Overlapping elements with a larger z-index
//! cover those with a smaller one.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The box does not establish a new local stacking context. The stack level of the generated
//! box in the current stacking context is `0`.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <integer> | inherit
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#propdef-z-index
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/z-index
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

